@startuml routre-lifecycle
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #1A1A1A
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam arrowColor #555555
skinparam arrowThickness 1.2
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam noteBorderColor #D4A017
skinparam noteFontColor #333333
skinparam noteFontSize 11
skinparam titleFontSize 17
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #999999
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderThickness 1.2
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantFontSize 12

title routre - request lifecycle (streaming and non-streaming, with failover)

actor "Client\n(opencode / Codex / Claude Code)" as Client
participant "HTTP Server\nnet/http" as HTTP
participant "Pipeline\nproxy.Pipeline" as Pipe
database "Cache\nLRU, SHA-256" as Cache
participant "Router\ntiers + cooldown" as Router
participant "candidateRunner\n+ dialect + relay" as Runner
database "Upstream\nProviders" as Up

== Steps 1-3 - detect, compress, key ==

Client -> HTTP : POST /v1/chat/completions\n/v1/messages /v1/responses  (JSON + stream flag)
HTTP -> Pipe : Request{body, path, header, client}
Pipe -> Pipe : **1 Format detect** from path + body\nresponses payload sanitized, kept native
Pipe -> Pipe : **2 RTK Apply** compresses tool text\n(11 filters, fail-open)
Pipe -> Pipe : **3 Prefix order** (cache.prefix_order)\nsystem messages first, stable prefix
Pipe -> Pipe : finish() - never-grow check\n+ key = v2:sha256(canonical JSON)

note right of Pipe
  If RTK somehow grew the body the
  envelope throws the mutation away
  and sends the original bytes, so the
  saved-token metric can never lie.
end note

== Step 4 - cache lookup ==

Pipe -> Cache : GetWithReason(key)
alt cache HIT and the stored shape matches the request
  Cache --> Pipe : Entry{body, sse, promptTokens}
  Pipe -> Pipe : usage.Record(cacheSaved = stored prompt tokens)\nmetrics.CacheHit()
  Pipe --> HTTP : 200 + X-Llrouter-Cache: hit
  HTTP --> Client : replayed SSE frames verbatim, or JSON\n**[no upstream call]**
else miss (disabled / absent / expired / shape_mismatch)
  Cache --> Pipe : miss reason
  Pipe -> Pipe : metrics.CacheMissReason(reason)
end

== Step 5 - candidates ==

Pipe -> Router : CandidatesWithFallbacks(model, fallbacks)
Router -> Router : drop providers cooling for this model\ntiers tried in config order
alt no candidate, but providers are cooling
  Router --> Pipe : MinCooldownForModel
  Pipe --> HTTP : 503 providers_unavailable\n+ Retry-After: cooldown left
else no candidate at all
  Pipe --> HTTP : 503 model_not_found
else candidates (tier 1 -> tier 2 -> tier 3)
  Router --> Pipe : Candidate{provider, baseURL, kind}
end
HTTP --> Client : error JSON, nothing was sent upstream

== Steps 6-7 - run, streaming shown ==

Pipe -> Runner : Run(ctx, candidates, eval)
note right of Runner
  The request gets one 30 s budget.
  Every untried candidate is guaranteed
  a fair slice of what is left, capped
  at 30 s, so one slow provider cannot
  eat the window of a healthy one.
end note

loop for each candidate, in tier order
  Runner -> Up : POST {base}/v1/{chat/completions,messages,responses}\nBearer key from keystore, body translated if cross-kind
  Up --> Runner : status + headers

  alt 401 / 403
    Runner -> Runner : refreshCredentials(re-read routre.env)
    alt key actually changed
      Runner -> Up : retry same provider, fresh key (no sleep)
    else key unchanged
      Runner -> Runner : outcome class=auth -> next candidate
    end
  else connection-level error (dial refused/reset)
    Runner -> Up : 1 retry, same provider, no sleep
  else 5xx / 429 / overloaded
    Runner -> Runner : outcome recorded, cooldown =\nmax(backoff, Retry-After capped 30s)\nnext candidate
  else 400 / 404 / 422
    Runner -> Runner : client error, no retry
    note right of Runner
      A deterministic upstream 4xx is
      surfaced verbatim instead of being
      dressed up as "all providers failed".
    end note
  else 200 success
    alt streaming
      Up --> Runner : SSE frames, translated in flight\n(Anthropic / OpenAI / Gemini state\nmachine, flushed frame by frame)
      Runner --> HTTP : flush to the client,\ncapture frames for the cache
      note right of Runner
        Emitted guard: once the first
        byte is out, failover stops -
        no duplicated output. A mid-stream
        abort is never cached.
      end note
    else non-streaming
      Up --> Runner : JSON body + usage{prompt, completion, cost}
    end
    Runner -> Router : success resets the cooldown
  end
end

== Outcome ==

alt every candidate failed
  Runner --> Pipe : TryLog[] of failures.Outcome
  Pipe -> Pipe : classify the round
  note right of Pipe
    all client errors -> **404** model_not_found
    all auth         -> **502** check the keys
    all out of credit-> **402** top up
    all overloaded   -> **503** Retry-After 1s
    mixed            -> **503** Retry-After 5s
    never tried      -> 503 + failover_budget outcome
  end note
  Pipe --> HTTP : error body with attempts[]\n(provider, kind, class, cooldown left)
  HTTP --> Client : honest error, same shape as `routre doctor`
else success
  Pipe -> Cache : Put(key, body or SSE)\n8 MiB per entry, 128 MiB total
  Pipe -> Pipe : usage.Record + cost\nreqlog phases: dial / headers / TTFB / total
  HTTP --> Client : 200 (stream finished, or JSON)
end

@enduml
